            <title>1.5.11</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 23:06:36 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>43</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.11</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Shift-click now selects a range in the icon views and the Gallery.</b> In the icon view modes (Extra Large through Small) and the Gallery, Shift-clicking only toggled the clicked item — like ⌘-click — instead of selecting everything between your last click and the clicked item, the way the List and Details views (and Windows Explorer) do. All views now select the contiguous range, and the anchor survives repeated Shift-clicks so you can widen or narrow the range.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
